{
  "ruleId": "CG-PART-SHORT-SLAB-LAND-BUILDING",
  "ruleSet": "RS-CG-PART",
  "_note": "A short-term gain on land or building falls outside the condition of S2 s.196(1)(b) (TY 2026-27, p.220) and 1961 s.111A(1)(b) (TY 2025-26, thc copy p.461), which reach a listed security sold with securities transaction tax, and no other special-rate provision charges it, so it is charged with the rest of total income (D-289; W-088g2, D-425). The provisions cited are the condition it fails; it has no charging section of its own. No securities transaction tax condition is carried: a transfer of land or building bears none, and a side whose charge breakdown records nothing reads UNKNOWN (D-292, CapitalGainsStt). Sources: docs/taxplanning-build/sources/2026-10-18-capital-gains-basis.md rows 1, 4–9.",
